lifeos-nix patch f-launcher-cwd — default to the current directory, not ~/.claude

PROBLEM
  The `lifeos` launcher (LIFEOS/TOOLS/lifeos.ts) chdir'd to the config root (~/.claude) before
  spawning Claude Code on EVERY launch, unless the user passed --local. So a session opened
  anywhere (a project, a dev dir) landed with cwd = ~/.claude — Claude sees the LifeOS config
  tree instead of the project the user is actually in. For a dev-first workflow that is the
  wrong default; the useful case (session in the config root for LifeOS-meta work) is the rare one.

FIX (invert the default)
  Default is now stay-in-current-directory. Opt in to the config root with --claude-dir / -c.
  --local is kept as a no-op alias for the now-default behavior (back-compat for existing use).
  Both the interactive launch (cmdLaunch) and the one-shot (cmdPrompt) paths honor this; the
  one-shot's unconditional chdir is removed. CLI flag, dispatch, help text, and docstring updated.

SCOPE / CO-EXISTENCE
  One file (lifeos.ts): cmdLaunch / cmdPrompt / arg-parse / help. Disjoint from f4-a, which
  touches only the update-check functions (getLatestVersion / cmdUpdate). No other patch
  touches lifeos.ts. Applied last, so the diff is against the f4-a-patched tree.

VERIFICATION
  `bun build --target bun` parses; hunks via diff -u. `lifeos` now stays in cwd; `lifeos -c`
  runs in ~/.claude; `lifeos --local` still works (no-op).

